When accessing the Google search results page directly, everything works fine in Headful mode — both in a regular browser and when connected via CDP.
However, when running the same setup in Headless mode, Google consistently returns a CAPTCHA instead of the normal search results.

This behavior is reproducible even without using any frameworks (pure Chrome command line).

⸻

Steps to Reproduce

✅ Works (Headful)

```
chrome.exe --remote-debugging-port=9222 --no-sandbox 
  --bot-profile="C:\Users\Admin\Documents\botbro5\win1.enc" 
  --remote-debugging-address=0.0.0.0 
  --user-data-dir="C:\Users\Admin\Documents\botbro5\userdata"
```

❌ Fails (Headless)

```
chrome.exe --remote-debugging-port=9222 --no-sandbox 
  --bot-profile="C:\Users\Admin\Documents\botbro5\win1.enc" 
  --remote-debugging-address=0.0.0.0 
  --user-data-dir="C:\Users\Admin\Documents\botbro5\userdata" 
  --headless=new
```

Result: Google returns a CAPTCHA instead of normal results.

⸻

Reproducible Example (via CDP)

```
(async () => {
  try {
    const browser = await chromium.connectOverCDP('Your CDP address here');

    const context = await browser.newContext({
      incognito: true
    });

    const page = await context.newPage();

    await page.goto('https://www.google.com/search?q=test', {
      waitUntil: 'networkidle'
    });

    const html = await page.content();
    console.log(html);

    await context.close();
    // await browser.close();
  } catch (error) {
    console.error('Error:', error);
  }
})();

```

⸻

Additional Notes

You can reproduce the same CAPTCHA response without any frameworks using this command:

```
chrome.exe --no-sandbox --disable-gpu --incognito 
  --bot-profile="C:\Users\Admin\Documents\botbro4\profiles\win1.enc"
  --headless 
  --disable-blink-features=AutomationControlled 
  --dump-dom "https://www.google.com/search?q=test"
```


⸻

Expected Behavior:

Google should return the same search results as in Headful mode.

Actual Behavior:

Google responds with a CAPTCHA page when running in Headless mode.

